course: dictionary
lesson: 12691
title: Many kinds of things
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Diversified means made more varied, with many different kinds of things instead of just one. «The farm grew only apples, but now it grows pears, plums and herbs too, so it is more diversified.» The farm did not stop growing apples. It just added other things, so it now has a wider mix.
explain: Diversified can be a verb or an adjective. As a verb, it is the past form of diversify: «The shop diversified last year and began selling hats.» As an adjective, it describes something, as in «a diversified business» or «a diversified economy». Look at the words around it to see which job it does.
explain: Business people often use this word. «The company made only toys, so when toy sales fell, it was in trouble. Then it diversified into books and games.» Now the company sells many products, so one bad sale does not ruin it.
fact: Diversified means made more varied, or spread across many different kinds of things.
fact: In business, diversified means having many products, jobs or investments instead of just one.
fact: «A diversified economy» is one with many kinds of jobs and industries, such as farming, tourism and shipping.
fact: Diversify is the verb, so «The farm diversified» means the farm changed to do more different things.
fact: Diversified often appears with «into», as in «The town diversified into tourism».
exercise: «The farm used to grow only apples. Now it grows pears, plums and herbs too.» Which word fits best: the farm has become ... | silent | *diversified | ancient | frozen
exercise: In «a diversified economy», what kind of economy is it? | One that is very quiet | One that has only one kind of job | One that is very old | *One with many different kinds of jobs and industries
exercise: Ben's family shop sold only shoes. Now it also sells bags, hats and socks. Which word describes the shop now? | Barely | Curt | Glum | *Diversified
test: «The island's economy depended only on fishing, so a bad season hurt everyone.» What would make the economy more diversified? | Fishing only, but catching more fish | Closing the harbour | Eating more fish | *Adding tourism, farming and shipping as well as fishing
test: Why might a business choose to diversify? | *So that if one product fails, it still has others | So that it sells only one thing very well | So that it becomes smaller | So that it stops changing
exam: «Over millions of years, life on Earth diversified into many species.» What does diversified mean here? | Grew very old quickly | Became very quiet | *Spread out into many different kinds | Stayed exactly the same
